// src/v4/extdeps/languages/ptx.dag
//
// Scope: CUDA model — direction-agnostic. Modeled at the PTX ISA layer
//        (recommended fork — see below): the SIMT execution model
//        (grid / block / thread / warp), the memory hierarchy
//        (global/shared/local/register), kernels and barriers.
// Anchor: NVIDIA "Parallel Thread Execution ISA" specification — pin a
//         version (e.g. PTX ISA 8.x) as the versioned fidelity authority
//         (L-2); the "CUDA C++ Programming Guide" documents the SIMT
//         execution model the spec encodes.
// Stress (T-4.14 — a B2-OMNI + IN-B falsification probe): the SIMT
//   data-parallel execution model. CUDA's grid/block/thread is massive
//   data-parallelism — does it fit the 5 L1 behaviors as effect-typed
//   Bind composition (the IN-B bet, like Verilog's concurrency), or does
//   it tempt a 6th `Parallel`/`Kernel` behavior? If it cannot be modeled
//   without one, that is a C1 stop-signal escalation — and catching it
//   early is exactly why this is added up front.
// Clear win: `.dag → PTX` (GPU kernels from one source, same Node as a
//   CPU backend), demonstrating omni-emission reaches the GPU.
//
// Fork (PROPOSED — operator confirm): model PTX (the spec'd IR — clean,
//   most general, captures SIMT directly, parallel to llvm_ir.dag —
//   recommended) vs CUDA-C++ as a `cpp.dag` extension (entangled with
//   cpp.dag; the C++ surface is not where the stress is). Recommend PTX.
//
// Owns:
//   - PTX grammar as declarative bidirectional data (B2-OMNI):
//     kernel / thread-hierarchy / memory-space / barrier / instruction
//   - SIMT parallelism as effect-typed Bind composition per IN-B — NOT a
//     new behavior (a 6th behavior here = C1 STOP, escalate)
//   - Inhabitance: PTX register/vector types per std/algebra.dag
//   - Cost realization: per-instruction + occupancy cost on a PTX target
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag, std/primitive.dag
//   - extdeps/coordination.dag (SIMT via effect-typed Bind — IN-B)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4.14
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.extdeps.languages.ptx
